Sigils are an element of casting seals, special designs drawn with [[Conjuring Ink|conjuring ink]] through which [[Magic|magic]] can be harnessed in the form of [[Spells|spells]]. Sigils are typically placed in the center of a seal and control what type of spell will be cast. For instance, the [[Pyreball Seal|Pyreball seal]] contains a Sigil of Fire and creates a floating ball of fire. 

The size of a sigil in relation to the ring determines the intensity and strength of the spell’s effect, with larger sigils creating more powerful effects compared to smaller ones.{{Ref|m|46|9-10}}{{Ref|a|6}} The placement of a sigil has not been stated or shown to have an effect on the spell, only serving as a way to more conveniently adjust and adapt typical spellcasting structure. It is possible for casting seals to make use of more than one sigil or lack a sigil altogether.
