==Decorative Sigils==
'''Decorative Sigils''' depict different kinds of flora and fauna. Using these, spells can be sculpted to take on the rough shape of its corresponding design, or target other spells shaped by the same sigil.{{Ref|m|58|22}}{{Ref|m|64|2}} They also allow spells to limit their effects to the physical counterparts of their respective designs.{{Ref|m|78|17-19}} '''Decorative Sigils''' take up a large amount of space inside a seal and lack practical utility, leading to most of them being lost to time or used in a witch's personal doodles.{{Ref|m|58|23}} '''Decorative Sigils''' were previously referred to as '''Decorative Signs''', up until this was retconned in Chapter 78.{{Ref|m|58|22}}{{Ref|m|62|10}} They are also referred to as '''Ornamental Sigils''' in the English translation of the World Guide.{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 150}}

